description: Git workflow for a solo project without pull requests or CI/CD
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git Workflow

- The primary branch is `main` (there is no `master` branch).
- Work directly in `main` unless the user explicitly requests a separate branch.
- Do not create pull requests. Commit completed work and push it directly to `origin/main`.
- Before pushing, run the relevant local lint, typecheck, test, and build checks because CI/CD is not configured.
- Pull remote updates with fast-forward only before starting new work when `main` is behind.
- Never force-push or rewrite published history unless the user explicitly requests it.
